{
 "note": "Cape Leeuwin Lighthouse (1895-96), from the Landgate aerial (Oct 2026), Wikipedia, the inHerit records and Lighthouses of Australia. Mainland Australia's tallest lighthouse: a 39 m round tower of local limestone, white, on a square base, seven floors with small windows, a gallery on the masonry at the sixth floor and a white 3.7 m (12 ft) Chance lantern with a domed cap and vent. The round, tapering tower is approximated by three tiers of stacked boxes (two crossed bars and a square each), so it reads as a stepped twelve-sided column; a true round tower, corbelled gallery and lantern want a Blender layer. Metres: x left to right as seen from the north (the car park and the cottages), y back (south).",
